{"ts": "2026-10-24T23:10:00", "task": "M4-explore-picker+weapon-reuse", "status": "ok", "commit": "f7e52c3", "note": "User ask: let the player choose which weapons to explore with, accounting for abilities that allow using a weapon more than once. TWO findings: (1) FEATURE - new pure client/src/ui/explorePicker.ts (exploreWeaponOptions/bestExploreCombo/evaluateExploreCombo/legalExplores) + ActionBar picker UI (Choose weapons toggle, per-weapon DMG/AMMO, live totals, reuse badge, Select all/Clear, disabled+reason when illegal). (2) ENGINE BUG - Leon L2 pistolsTwicePerTurn was unreachable: validateAction allowed reusing a play-area pistol but enumerateLegalActions built combos from hand weapons only, so the 2nd use was never offered (client OR bot). Fixed by new engine/weaponReuse.ts (weaponUsesThisTurn/maxWeaponUses/remainingWeaponUses/canReuseWeapon/explorableWeapons) shared by validate+enumerate+UI; pool is now hand weapons + reusable play-area weapons. canReuseWeapon requires a reuse ability to actually apply (play-area weapon w/o ability is NOT reusable just because a use is available). Per-weapon ammo now ability-aware (Leon L1 pistol -10). Tests +8 engine, +4 client. Browser-verified against dev server: picker live totals 10->5 dmg, Clear disables w/ reason, full explore dispatches to engine (log + hand 5->3). Gates: typecheck x3, 641 tests (core 429/client 126/server 86), vite build green."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T09:10:00", "task": "hand-card z-order fix", "status": "ok", "note": "User reported overlapping hand cards painted wrong: card name + cost badge of an earlier card rendered on top of the card covering it. Root cause: .hand-card <button> was position:static, so its inner .card-top/.card-name (z-index:1) escaped into the hand's stacking context and painted above every later card's body (positive z-index beats auto). Fix: .hand-card { position: relative; z-index: 0 } makes each card its own stacking context - later cards overlap earlier ones in DOM order, and the existing :hover z-index:2 now actually lifts the hovered card (it was a no-op before). Browser-verified against dev server (pass & play, First Timer): elementFromPoint over card1's cost badge inside card2's body returns card2 with the fix; injecting the old static positioning reproduces the bug (returns card1's .card-cost). Gates: client 126 tests green, typecheck green x3. Pre-existing red at HEAD, unrelated: game-core cards.test.ts data invariants (db size 81 vs 65, alliance missing from set union, mansion population 70 vs 33 - Outbreak commit 32867a9 added cards without updating them) and server integration gameOver-during-bot-step."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T09:36:00", "task": "fix card data invariants + server integration test", "status": "ok", "note": "cards.test.ts had 3 red invariants at HEAD (db size 81 vs 65, set-union missing alliance, mansion population 70 vs 33). Root cause: commit 87eca33 added 16 Alliance infected (ma-022..ma-037, set alliance) into PREMIER_CARDS in cards.ts, duplicating the canonical entries already in alliance.ts (fc8e4fe, 8h earlier). Fix: removed the 16 duplicates from PREMIER_CARDS (restores 65 unique, sets premier/promo, infected 33 + tokens 2 + herb 3 = 38 = STANDARD_MANSION_DECK) and merged their machine-readable infectedEffects into the 6 canonical alliance.ts entries (ma-023 plusHpIfAttackedWithAnotherInfected, ma-025 onKillGainAmmoX10ToMostDecorated, ma-029 buffOtherRevealedInfected, ma-030 mustExploreNextTurnOnDefeat, ma-035 plusHpAndDamagePerAttachedInfected, ma-036 trashHighestCostAttachedOnPartnerIfNotExactDefeat) so no data was lost and Alliance games now actually carry the effects the engine wiring in explore.ts expects. Also: deleted committed debug probe game-core/src/probe_alliance.test.ts; removed leftover stepBot console.log from server/src/host.ts (e7fe47f); re-pinned server integration test seed 109 -> 19 (109 was the original gameOver-on-bot-step repro but bot-policy/mansion-deck changes made it a stall seed - verified identical stall with pre-change data; seeds 9/10/11/13/18/19 end with uroborosDefeated on a bot step, 19 chosen at turn ~15). Remaining known issue (pre-existing, not touched): ALL_CARDS still has 17 duplicate ids (we-001..we-016, it-001) where alliance.ts re-prints base cards with set alliance - definitions are functionally identical (alliance copies only add empty weaponEffects), defsById is last-wins so Alliance games use the alliance copies; harmless but worth deduping someday. Gates: game-core 429, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T10:46:00", "task": "implement Nightmare Ada L1 (cardsOnDamageTakenDuringTurn)", "status": "ok", "note": "First of the 4 missing character abilities. Card text (fandom CH-043, verified): 'During your turn, if Ada takes damage, you get +2 cards'. Implementation: applyAction is now a thin wrapper over applyActionInternal + applyDamageTakenHooks, a post-action pass that compares each seat HP before/after and draws the ability amount when the seat took damage while it was that seat's turn. Chosen over sprinkling the hook through the 6+ damage sites (explore reveal, pending explore resolution, MA-037/MA-031 reveal AoE, Explosive Barrel, action effects) so every current and future damage source is covered by one choke point. Guard: skip the draw when the seat is downed/dead - a downed character has no hand and revive redraws one, so drawing there would silently drop the cards. Level gating comes free via characterAbilities (level 0 -> no draw). Tests: +3 actions.test.ts (positive draw, level-0/no-ability control, downed no-draw) and +1 abilities.test.ts helper unit test. Gates: game-core 433, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T10:55:00", "task": "implement Nightmare Ada L2 (setHpToOnLethal)", "status": "ok", "note": "Card text (fandom CH-043): 'When Ada health would be reduced to 0 or less, set it to 10 instead.' User rulings: (1) applies EVERY time (literal text) - she can never be downed; (2) L2 replaces the damage, so no HP is lost and L1 (+2 cards on damage during your turn) does NOT trigger on a clamped hit - which the HP-decrease-based L1 hook already satisfies. Implementation: new abilities.ts helpers setHpToOnLethal + applyHpLoss(abilities, hp, amount, seatDownedOrDead); all 7 damage sites in actions.ts now route through applyHpLoss (explore infected attack incl. leading-partner guard, MA-037 Guardian of Insanity AoE, MA-031 Proto Tyrant AoE, MA-038 Explosive Barrel, action effects damageCharacter/elseDamageAndDraw, deferred pending-explore resolution). The clamp runs before the downed check so a clamped hit never downs her. Guard: seatDownedOrDead skips the replacement so stray AoE cannot revive an already-downed Ada for free. Level gating free via characterAbilities (L2 needs level 2). Tests: +3 actions.test.ts (lethal clamp, non-lethal unaffected + level-gated control, MA-037 AoE clamp) and +2 abilities.test.ts (applyHpLoss replacement/guard unit tests). Note: typecheck caught a widened string literal in the test fixture that vitest (esbuild, no typecheck) let through - thema-037 def needed an explicit CardDef type. Gates: game-core 438, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T11:00:00", "task": "implement Nightmare Luis Sera L2 (onDefeatMoveDiscardToInventoryBottom)", "status": "ok", "note": "Card text (fandom CH-036): 'once Luis defeats an Infected, the player can move any number of cards from their discard pile to the bottom of the Inventory.' Implementation: new prompt kind luisSeraDiscardToInventory, chained like Rebecca L2 trashFromHandAtWill (options = discard instance ids + DONE, each pick moves one card and re-prompts). Builder lives in the explore defeated branch: gated by movesDiscardToInventoryOnDefeat(characterAbilities(state, seat)) and only when the discard is non-empty, so an empty discard or a locked tier creates no prompt. Resolver appends the chosen id to the inventory array - the draw pile draws from index 0, so the end IS the bottom. Bots get the choice for free: enumerateLegalActions already emits every chooseOption option and the ActionBar renders any prompt generically, so no UI/bot work. Tests: +3 actions.test.ts (prompt appears on defeat, move-to-bottom + chain + DONE, empty-discard/level-gated no-prompt) and +1 abilities.test.ts helper test. Gates: game-core 442, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T11:09:00", "task": "implement Nightmare Wesker L2 (choosePlayerToDiscardOneCardDuringTurn)", "status": "ok", "note": "Last of the 4 missing character abilities. Card text (fandom CH-041): L1 'if only one other player character has 30 or less health, you may choose to get +1 card'; L2 'During your turn, you may choose to have the aforementioned player discard one card.' Implementation rides the existing manual-ability seam: validate.ts accepts the kind in the once-per-turn manual block with a condition requiring EXACTLY one other living player at <=30 HP who holds a card; actions.ts useCharacterAbility case creates the prompt. User ruling: the VICTIM picks the discarded card, so the prompt is addressed to the victim's seat (seat: target.seat) and resolved out of turn by that player's client - same per-seat prompt pattern as the Jill Flash Grenade reactive window. Once-per-turn log scan prevents draining a hand in one turn (ability is otherwise free). enumerateLegalActions needed no change (it already emits useCharacterAbility for every ability index). Known limitation (accepted): in pass & play the shared screen never shows another seat's prompt, so the effect silently does not resolve there - same limitation the reactive window already has. Tests: +3 actions.test.ts (prompt goes to the victim seat with their hand, victim discards the chosen card + once-per-turn rejection, no-target and level-gated rejection). Gates: game-core 445, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T11:24:00", "task": "implement Alliance CH-018 Leon + CH-017 Billy character abilities", "status": "ok", "note": "Continuing the character-card implementation with the Alliance characters whose text AND gates are verified against the fandom wiki (the in-repo alliance.ts text is unreliable - see the report). CH-018 Leon S. Kennedy: L1 discardCardToInventoryBottom (manual, prompt picks the discard card, appended to the inventory array = draw-pile bottom), L2 inventoryBottomToTop (manual, deterministic: last inventory card to index 0). CH-017 Billy Coen: L1 gainAmmoX10ForGold (manual, finds the market pile whose TOP card is am-001 Ammo x10, moves it to the discard per the gain rule, +10 gold), L2 discardToHandIfTenPlus (manual, prompt picks a discard card to move to hand, gated on discard >= 10). Both characters also got their empty levels[] arrays filled so the UI skill rows render. validate gates: once-per-turn log scan shared with the other manual abilities, plus per-ability preconditions (non-empty discard/inventory, Ammo x10 in market, 10+ discard). Tests: +6 actions.test.ts. Gates: game-core 451, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T11:28:00", "task": "implement Alliance CH-014 Jack Krauser character abilities", "status": "ok", "note": "CH-014 had text but empty levels/abilities. L1 'cannot use more than one weapon' maps to the EXISTING singleWeaponLimiter kind (already enforced in validate explore + enumerate combo generation), so it was a data-only addition; level1At corrected 1 -> 0 per the wiki prose ('activated at the beginning of the game due to a cost of 0'). L2 '+10 damage per card in hand' is a new passive kind plusDamagePerCardInHand; passiveDamageBonus gained a handCount parameter and BOTH compute sites now pass it (actions.ts explore apply path and explore.ts exploreDamage, so the mansion-reveal overlay number matches the resolved number). Data caveat: the L2 gate (6) comes only from the spreadsheet-derived alliance.ts and is unverified against a card scan - flagged for the user. Tests: +2 actions.test.ts (limiter rejects a 2-weapon explore; exploreDamage 10 base + 10 x 4 cards = 50 and a 20 HP infected is defeated; level-gated at L1). Gates: game-core 453, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T11:41:00", "task": "implement Alliance CH-013 Steve Burnside character abilities", "status": "ok", "note": "alliance.ts text for CH-013 was wrong ('Begins the game with an Explosive weapon'); corrected to the wiki wording. L1 healAtTurnStart (passive, 10 HP at each turn start) is a new helper consumed in game.ts startTurn, added to the existing hp computation alongside the Yellow Herb debt and capped at maxHp. L2 discardCardForHealAndDamage (manual, payload cardId ac-018 / heal 20 / damage 30): validate requires the named card in hand plus the shared once-per-turn scan; apply moves it from hand to discard, heals (capped) and adds +damage to weaponDamageBonusThisTurn (the engine's per-turn base-damage field). Data caveat: gates 5/7 are spreadsheet-only and unverified. Tests: +2 actions.test.ts (turn-start heal incl. max-HP cap; L2 discard/heal/damage + rejection without the card). Gates: game-core 455, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T11:48:00", "task": "implement Alliance CH-019 Chris Redfield character abilities", "status": "ok", "note": "alliance.ts text reworded to the wiki. L1 singleWeaponAmmoDiscount (passive, -20 ammo only when the explore uses exactly one weapon) and L2 chosenWeaponTypeAmmoDiscount (manual, player picks a weapon type; new PlayerState field chrisAmmoDiscountTypes, reset at turn start in game.ts). Both discounts are applied in THREE places so the charged ammo and the displayed number agree: the explore requiredAmmo reduce (this was the bug the tests caught - the reduce originally bypassed the discount), the exploreWeapons map used for damage, and explore.ts exploreDamage for the mansion-reveal overlay. validate: L2 is in the manual once-per-turn block and requires at least one typed weapon in hand/play area; L1 is passive (rejected by the default manual case). Data caveat: gates 3/8 are spreadsheet-only and unverified. Tests: +2 actions.test.ts (L1 discount only with one weapon; L2 prompt -> type recorded -> discount applied -> reset next turn; rejection without a typed weapon). Gates: game-core 457, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T11:56:00", "task": "implement Alliance CH-016 Jill Valentine (Brainwashed)", "status": "ok", "note": "L1 partnerAttachedCountDamageBonus (passive, +10 explore damage when her partner has <=1 attached card; no partner -> no bonus) wired into BOTH the explore apply path and exploreDamage so the overlay number matches. L2 offTurnFlashGrenadeLasPlagas was already implemented but keyed on the card id (ch-016) in TWO places (the reactive-window builder and the shouldDefer condition); encoded the ability in the data and switched both checks to characterAbilities, so the data now drives who may react (a different character with the ability would also react). levels[] filled. Data caveat: gates 1/6 are spreadsheet-only and unverified. Tests: +2 actions.test.ts (L1 bonus with 0/2 attached and no partner; L2 reactive prompt fires for an ability holder and NOT for a different character, proving the check is no longer id-based). Also extended the test seat() helper to pass partner fields (it previously dropped them, which is why the first run failed). Gates: game-core 459, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T11:59:00", "task": "implement Alliance CH-012 Josh Stone + fix his wrong ability", "status": "ok", "note": "CH-012 was encoded with singleWeaponLimiter (Krauser's ability) and text 'Begins the game with a Knife and an Action card'. Corrected to the wiki: L1 cannot use weapons costing 50 or more (gate 0), L2 partner may attach up to 2 additional cards (gate 4). L1 weaponCostCap is enforced in THREE places so UI and bots cannot offer an explore validate would reject: validate explore, enumerateLegalActions (the shared weapon pool for the ActionBar AND bots), and the helpers module. L2 partnerAttachCapBonus required replacing the hardcoded partner attach cap of 2 in all THREE sites that enforce it: validate attachToPartner (replaceIndex validity now 0..cap-1), the attachToPartner apply path, and the AC-013/014/020 auto-attach path. New shared helpers weaponCostCap + partnerAttachCap in abilities.ts. Data caveat: gates 0/4 ARE wiki-verified. Tests: +2 actions.test.ts (cost cap rejects/enum excludes an expensive weapon; attach cap raised to 4 with replaceIndex required only when full, base cap unchanged for other characters). Gates: game-core 461, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T12:12:00", "task": "implement Alliance CH-020 Claire Redfield", "status": "ok", "note": "L1 herbTrashDamageBonus (+20 damage this turn when a Green or Red Herb is trashed from hand) and L2 doubleDamageOnBothHerbs (double ALL damage this turn when a Green and a Red Herb are both trashed - i.e. the Red Herb path, which trashes a Green from hand too). New PlayerState field damageMultiplierThisTurn, reset at all 3 turn-start sites in game.ts. The multiplier is applied in ONE place - the tail of computeDamage (Math.round(damage * mult)) - and plumbed from both consumers (exploreDamage for the overlay number, resolveExplore for the real outcome, so a doubled explore can defeat an infected that would otherwise survive). Herb identity is detected by itemEffects kind, not card id, so it follows the data. levels[] filled. Data caveat: gates 3/7 are spreadsheet-only and unverified. Tests: +3 actions.test.ts (L1 +20 on a herb trash and reflected in exploreDamage; L2 doubles, L1 still stacks, a character without the abilities gets neither; multiplier + bonus reset at the next turn start). Gates: game-core 464, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T12:24:00", "task": "implement Alliance CH-011 Carlos Oliveira + correct his text", "status": "ok", "note": "Re-fetched the wiki page (Carlos Oliveira (CH-011)) and confirmed the existing data text was WRONG - it carried Ada's L1 ('if it is a Weapon, you may take it') and Josh's L2 ('attach up to 2 additional cards'). Corrected to: L1 look at the top card of the Mansion Area before playing weapons to Explore (gate 4), L2 take a card from the Discard Pile to hand if the damage dealt to all Revealed Infected equals their health (gate 9). L1 reuses the existing revealMansionTopNoEffect kind (the wiki says it is similar to Ada Wong's), so no new engine code. L2 perfectExploreReward: resolveExplore's defeated outcome now also carries the EFFECTIVE damage dealt and the effective HP (two existing exact-equality tests updated for the new fields), and the explore defeated branch offers a choose-one-discard prompt when damage === hp and the discard is non-empty; the chooseOption handler moves the chosen card to hand. levels[] filled. Data caveat: gates 4/9 are spreadsheet-only and unverified. Tests: +3 actions.test.ts (L1 peek prompt; L2 perfect explore offers the prompt and the chosen card lands in hand; L2 overkill offers no prompt). Gates: game-core 467, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T13:10:00", "task": "Outbreak mode foundation: infection system, scenario, attack action", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 1 of wiring Outbreak into a playable scenario (user chose this over characters-first). Built from the RE3 rulebook (docs/rules/RE3_Rulebook.pdf, downloaded from the dropbox link the wiki cites; text extracted with pdftotext -layout). INFECTION: Infection Level is modelled exactly as the rulebook defines it - a face-up pile of Infection cards next to the Character (PlayerState.infectionCards, level = length), drawn from a new GameState.infectionDeck (IN-001..IN-007, 40 cards). End of turn: +1 if the active Player did not Explore the Mansion or Attack an Infected Character (PlayerState.exploredOrAttackedThisTurn, set by a new post-action hook in applyAction so it cannot drift). Reaching the Maximum Infection Level (10) kills the Character, shuffles their cards (including the face-up Infections) into the Inventory and marks pendingReanimate; startTurn then reanimates them as a random Zombie (ch-031/032/033) with 0 Buys / 0 Actions / 1 Explore. SCENARIO: new OUTBREAK_SCENARIO_DEF ('outbreak') with the rulebook's Outbreak resource piles and MA-041..MA-057 mansion; registered in ScenarioId/SCENARIOS, wired into server protocol+host and client hotseat, and ALL_CARDS now includes OUTBREAK_CARDS. WIN CONDITION: new GameState.endInfectedCardId + checkWin branch - the game ends when Tyrant T-002 (ma-041) is Defeated. ATTACK: new attack action spending 1 Explore; non-Infected attackers name a weapon (pays its ammo), Infected attackers deal their base Damage (new CardDef.baseDamage, Zombie A/B/C = 0/5/10) and a surviving Infected Character deals its base Damage back. Validated + enumerated so the UI and bots can offer it. Note: the Outbreak action/infected card EFFECTS (ac-023..ac-031, ma-041..ma-053) are still unimplemented - deferred to the next milestone. Also: the rulebook lists a 'Proximity Mine' in Kevin Ryman's Mercenary-mode starting inventory but no such DBG card exists in our data or on the wiki - flagged as a data gap. Gates: game-core 475, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T13:45:00", "task": "Outbreak infected-card effects (infection mechanics)", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 2a. Encoded and implemented the infection-related Infected effects so Outbreak mode actually progresses. New InfectedEffect kinds: onRevealInfectionIncrease (MA-042 Yawn: +2 at level<=5 else +1), onRevealAllInfectionIncrease (MA-043 Nemesis: every living character +1), onNotDefeatedInfectionIncrease (MA-041 Tyrant T-002: +1+level, MA-046 Web Spinner: +1), onNotDefeatedShuffleBack (MA-041), onDefeatInfectionIncrease+toMansionBottom (MA-053 Lisa Trevor: +1 then to the Mansion bottom, NOT attached). A reveal-effect block in the explore path draws infection cards from the deck into a per-seat map (drawInfectionsFor) and both the defeated and not-defeated returns write the map back for EVERY seat, not just the explorer - the first test run caught that MA-043 only infected the exploring character. MA-041 shuffle-back sets a flag so the default sendToBottom is skipped (no double move). Data encoded for ma-041/042/043/046/053. NOT done (deferred): MA-045 Wasp (reveal damage), MA-047 Reinforced Zombie (attached -1 level-2 gate), MA-048 Crimson Head (+10 hp/dmg with a Zombie attached), MA-049 Reinforced Licker (0-ammo weapons deal 0) - these are combat modifiers, not infection. Also noticed the Outbreak data has we-029 named 'Lightning Hawk' and we-030 'Hand Cannon [L. Hawk]', matching the rulebook's WE-029 & WE-030 pairing. Gates: game-core 480, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T14:20:00", "task": "Outbreak action cards: AC-023/024/027/028/030", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 2b. Completed/implemented five more Outbreak action cards. AC-023 Power of the t-Virus: +20 damage was already hardcoded; added the 'Trash for +20 Gold' prompt (the prompt now carries its instanceId so the trash can find the card) and the end-of-turn +1 Infection when the player explored or attacked an Infected Character - checked by looking for ac-023 in the play area before the end-of-turn discard. AC-024 'I Have This...': +1 card/+1 action already hardcoded; added the optional reveal of a weapon costing 50+ from hand for +1 card. AC-027 By Any Means Necessary: +2 Actions and a net -1 Infection Level ('decrease by any amount, then increase by the same amount minus one' always nets -1, so no prompt needed). AC-028 Higher Priorities: new returnedFavor-style choice prompt, +3 cards or +2 actions. AC-030 Returned Favor: +2 cards, attaches to the character (removed from the play area), and at the start of the next turn draws +1 card then discards itself - handled by a recursive startTurn call after the card is removed from attached so it cannot loop. Still NOT implemented: AC-026 Injection's discard-any-number/draw-the-same (only its +1 Action is done), AC-029 Parting Ways and AC-031 The Gathering Darkness (no engine support at all). Note: AC-027/028/030 are not in the rulebook's base 'Outbreak' scenario piles (they belong to the Infection Balance / Duplicity / Embrace the Darkness scenarios), so the tests register their instances explicitly. Also fixed a self-inflicted syntax error: appending returnedFavor after higherPriorities left the union's terminating semicolon in place. Gates: game-core 485, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T14:55:00", "task": "Outbreak action cards: AC-026 / AC-029 / AC-031", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 2c - the last three Outbreak action cards. AC-026 Injection: +1 Action plus a chained discard prompt (each chosen card is discarded, DONE draws the same amount, the running count carried in the prompt payload) followed by an optional trash for -1 Infection Level. AC-029 Parting Ways: +1 Action, optionally trash a hand card, then a second prompt offering the Resource Area cards costing up to (trashed cost + 20). AC-031 The Gathering Darkness: choose another player, trash this card, they trash their highest-cost Ammunition and gain one Ammo x10 into hand per 10 ammo it provided (via gainCard). Action-card prompts now always carry the played instanceId so trash/remove handlers can find the card (AC-023 was the first user). Data: ac-029/030/031 had empty actionEffects - encoded partingWays / returnedFavor / gatheringDarkness, and added the missing +1 Action for AC-029. All 11 Outbreak action cards now have engine behaviour except that AC-023/024/026 still partly ride on hardcoded def.id checks rather than their effect kinds. Gates: game-core 488, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T15:25:00", "task": "Outbreak infection cards (IN-001..IN-007) in the attack path", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 2d - the Infection cards, which are what make Infected Characters a threat. The attack action now takes infectionCardIds, playable only by Infected Characters and only from hand (validated). Data encodes each card's damage on CardDef.damage plus a new ActionEffect kind: infectionActionsNextTurn (IN-001 Claw 10 dmg + cap the target at 1 Action next turn), virulentFrenzy (IN-002), bileVomit (IN-003 5 dmg + 5 per other Bile Vomit used), sloughArmor (IN-004, still reactive - NOT implemented), drag (IN-005 - the target cannot attack back next turn), devour (IN-006 5 dmg + heal own infected character 20), infectionIncrease (IN-007 - the target gains 1 Infection Level, drawn from the deck). Two new PlayerState flags carry the next-turn effects (actionsCapNextTurn, cannotAttackSeatNextTurn); startTurn applies the action cap and clears both flags, and validate rejects an attack the Drag flag forbids. enumerateLegalActions offers the infection cards alongside the plain attack. IN-002 Virulent Frenzy and IN-004 Slough Armor are encoded in the data but have no engine behaviour yet (Virulent Frenzy needs the inventory top-3 trash flow, Slough Armor is a reactive discard during someone else's attack). Gates: game-core 493, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T16:05:00", "task": "Outbreak characters: CH-024 Mark, CH-027 Ada, CH-028 Chris, CH-030 Hunk", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 3a - the first four Outbreak characters. CH-024 Mark Wilkins: L1 plusDamageIfTwoOrMoreWeapons (+10 with 2+ weapons), L2 reuses weaponTagPlusDamage with the melee tag (+10 to every Melee weapon, which the Combat Knife/Survival Knife/Submission carry). CH-028 Chris Redfield: L1 discardAnyForAmmo (chained discard prompt, running count in the payload, +20 Ammo each on DONE; registered as a manual once-per-turn ability) and L2 exploreBonusIfAmmoAbove (+20 explore damage when he has over 100 ammo, evaluated against the pre-explore turnAmmo). CH-027 Ada Wong: L1 turnStartActionIfHpAtMost (+1 Action at turn start at <=30 Health, stacked on top of the IN-001 action cap); her gates 3/7 are wiki-verified. CH-030 Hunk: L2 baseDamageBonusIfHpAtMost (+30 base Damage at <=10 Health), applied in BOTH attack branches so it stacks with a weapon for non-Infected attackers and with the Zombie base damage. GATES: the wiki gives no decoration requirements for Mark/Chris/Hunk (or Excella/Kevin L2/David/Rebecca), BGG thread 574996 is Cloudflare-blocked and the rulebook text layer has no character table - so their level1At/level2At are set to undefined (character starts at level 1, L2 unreachable) and each line is tagged // GATES UNVERIFIED rather than inventing numbers. exploreDamage (the overlay helper) needed the same two bonuses added as the apply path - the tests caught that the overlay disagreed with the real damage. Also corrected two HP values the wiki contradicts: CH-029 Rebecca 70 -> 80, CH-032 Zombie B 140 -> 150. Gates: game-core 499, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T16:50:00", "task": "Outbreak characters: CH-021 Excella, CH-025 Jill, CH-026 Leon, CH-030 Hunk L1, CH-027 Ada L2", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 3b. CH-025 Jill Valentine (gates 3/6 wiki-verified): L1 turnStartDecreaseInfection - at turn start her Infection Level drops by 1 and the face-up Infection goes to the BOTTOM of the Infection Deck, per the rulebook; L2 immuneToInfectionAtLevelZero - while her level is 0 she is immune to infection effects, enforced by a new isImmuneToInfectionEffects helper checked at ALL THREE infection-draw sites (end of turn, the explore reveal effects per seat, and IN-007 in the attack path) so it cannot be bypassed. CH-026 Leon S. Kennedy (gates 1/7 wiki-verified): L1 moveHandCardToTopOfInventory and L2 discardForActionFromDiscard (discard one card, then move an action card from the discard to hand) - both manual, chained prompts. CH-021 Excella Gionne: L1 gainInfectionForGold (+1 Infection Level for +20 Gold, manual) and L2 turnStartCardsIfInfectionAtLeast (+3 cards at level 8+). CH-030 Hunk L1 turnStartDamageForExplore (take 10 Damage at turn start for +1 Explore) via the turnStartAbilityPrompts machinery. CH-027 Ada L2 turnStartRevealActionsForCards (reveal any number of action cards for +1 card each, chained prompt with the running count in the payload). Two bugs my tests caught: the reveal re-prompt offered only action cards with no DONE (chooseOption rejected -1), and TS narrowing on the Excella filter/reduce needed an explicit loop. Gates: game-core 507, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T17:20:00", "task": "Outbreak character CH-022 Kevin Ryman", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 3c. Kevin Ryman L1 gainSpecificWeaponIntoInventory (gate 0, wiki-verified): takes a Samurai Edge from the Resource Area when the top card of a pile is one, otherwise creates it from outside the game, and shuffles it into the Inventory with the seeded RNG. L2 movePlayAreaWeaponToInventoryTop (gate unknown -> undefined, tagged // L2 GATE UNVERIFIED): offers the Pistol-tagged weapons in the Play Area and moves the chosen one to the top of the Inventory. Both registered as manual once-per-turn abilities. Gates: game-core 509, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T17:55:00", "task": "Outbreak character CH-023 David King", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 3d - the hardest character in the set. L1 discardWeaponToCopyEffects: a manual ability that discards a weapon from hand, then offers the remaining hand/play-area weapons as targets; the discarded weapon's weaponEffects are serialised into the prompt payload and stored on the new PlayerState.copiedWeaponEffects for the turn. Both the apply path and exploreDamage merge those effects into the chosen weapon's entry. L2 knifeFromDiscardForExplore: when the explore uses a Knife-tagged weapon, one Knife from the discard pile is added to the explore at no ammo cost, in both the apply path and exploreDamage. Two findings while testing: (1) computeDamage implements only 8 of the declared WeaponEffect kinds - plusDamageIfSelfHpAtLeast (Submission WE-003), plusDamagePerCardGainedThisTurn (Samurai Edge WE-027) and plusDamagePerNonItemGainedThisTurn (Standard Sidearm WE-026) are declared but have NO engine code, so the L1 test uses the Survival Knife's plusDamagePerKnifeUsed instead; (2) the Nightmare cards are not in ALL_CARDS, so a Mine Thrower copied in an Outbreak game resolves to no def at all - worth remembering for cross-set scenarios. Gates: game-core 511, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T18:25:00", "task": "Outbreak character CH-029 Rebecca Chambers", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 3e - completes the character work. The user supplied the physical card, which overrides the wiki on two points: Health is 70 (not 80 as the wiki says) and the L2 text is now complete. L1 turnStartDiscardForInfection (gate 3, card-verified): a chained turn-start prompt; each discarded card lowers the Infection Level by 1, the removed face-up Infections go to the bottom of the Infection Deck. L2 drawWhenOtherInfectionDecreases (gate 6, card-verified): when an effect lowers ANOTHER character's Infection Level, Rebecca draws +1 card - wired at all three decrease sites (Jill L1 at turn start, AC-026 Injection trash, AC-027 By Any Means Necessary). Bug found and fixed: startTurn's final return rebuilt seats from the original state.seats, so a draw for a non-active seat was silently discarded; added a turnSeats variable that the return now uses. All 47 characters in the four sets now have engine behaviour (the three Zombies have none by design). Gates: game-core 514, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T14:45:00", "task": "gainCard refactor + AC-021 Gathering Forces", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 4a - gainCard refactor per docs/GAIN_CARD_REFACTOR_PLAN.md. gainCard.ts v2: instanceId moves an existing instance (buy, knife) instead of minting a duplicate; shuffleIntoInventory for Kevin Ryman L1; typed GainReason union; PlayerState.gainedCardsGoToHand is now a real field (was an as-any read); the on-gain hook draw uses drawWithReshuffle so an empty inventory reshuffles. Migrated every remaining inline gain site: market buy (removed the rollback hack that left stale gainedThisTurn ids), upgradeAmmoBy30Gold, token gainWeaponAndTrashToken, gainKnifeAtTurnStart, gainSpecificWeaponIntoInventory, partingWaysGain. AC-021 Gathering Forces is implemented for the first time: data carries actionEffects gainedCardsGoToHand, the effect sets the flag, and all three startTurn paths clear it (previously the flag was read but never set, so the effect was dead). New tests: gainCard.test.ts (8) and gainHooks.test.ts (4) covering destinations, count, instanceId moves, shuffle, Gathering routing, and Leon Nightmare L2 firing on buy/token/ability gains. Gates: game-core 526, server 89, client 126, typecheck exit 0."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T15:20:00", "task": "Card art in the UI (CARD-ART SVGs)", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 4b - card art in the UI. The scans in game-core/src/data/CARD-ART (25 files, UPPERCASE-ID.svg) are art-only (decorative border, no printed text) and full-card-proportioned, so they are used as the card FACE. New client/src/ui/cardArt.ts resolves them with an eager import.meta.glob over the game-core directory (query ?url, keyed by uppercased id): dropping a new SVG there is enough, Vite dedupes byte-identical files (AM-001/002/003 are identical - 23 assets emitted for 25 files), and the browser only fetches what a card renders. CardView switches on cardArtUrl(def.id): non-character cards get card-has-art (transparent frame, full-bleed cover img, text rows on a bottom scrim pinned with margin-top auto), character cards fill the card-portrait window so the skill list survives; cards without art keep the placeholder frame. MansionReveal no longer paints the art as a wrapper background (CardView does it now). Deleted the stale client/public/card-art copy (17 of 25 files, one differing). Layout: art mode is now layout-neutral vs the placeholder frame and card-text clamps to 3 lines (hover popup exempt) - probed all 25 art cards and the non-character overflow went from 12 cards (up to 58px) to 0. Caveat: the scans are 2-6MB each, dist is 68MB, and full-page screenshots of an art-card board time out in the browser harness. Gates: game-core 526, server 89, client 128 (2 new CardView art tests), typecheck exit 0, vite build ok."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T15:26:10", "task": "M5-T01 README + run scripts", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 5a - README.md (154 lines: requirements, dev/prod quick start, online/hotseat/bot modes, 8 scenarios, 4 card sets and 47 characters, workspace architecture, CARD-ART pipeline, test + deployment commands, known limitations) and root package.json scripts dev:client / dev:server / start. Verified: JSON parses, npm ls --depth 0 lists all four workspaces, baseline gates green (game-core 526, server 89, client 128, typecheck exit 0)."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T15:30:42", "task": "M5-T02 production build + deploy smoke test", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 5b - client production build verified (tsc --noEmit clean, vite build 68M dist, 25 hashed assets). New tools/smoke.mjs drives the real server entry (server/src/main.ts) against that build in single-port mode: /healthz 200, / serves index.html, hashed js/css/svg assets with correct MIME, extensionless route SPA fallback, missing asset 404, no static-root escape, and a live WS round trip (welcome+reconnectToken -> createRoom -> roomState with a seated player). 12/12 green via npm run smoke -- --port 18080. Root script smoke added; README documents it."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T15:37:36", "task": "M5-T03 reconnect torture test", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 5c - new server/src/reconnect.test.ts (7 tests) + shared server/src/testHelpers.ts (extracted from integration.test.ts so the suite does not duplicate the waiter machinery). Coverage: invalid token, token after leave (empty room is deleted), spectator token, mid-game resume (live stateSync, own hand visible, turn NOT lost, seat can act), stale-socket replacement, 20x reconnect churn (exactly one human player, still connected), and no silent bot takeover while disconnected. Found and FIXED a real bug in ws.ts: reconnect did byClient.set(clientId, ws) without retiring the previous socket, so a stale socket still held the session clientId - it could send actions as the player and its close handler marked the player disconnected even though the fresh socket was live (churn test caught it: connected:false after 20 reconnects). Fix: terminate the previous socket on reconnect, and guard the close handler with byClient.get(clientId) === ws so only the CURRENT socket clears routing / calls disconnectPlayer. Gates: typecheck exit 0, game-core 526, server 96 (+7), client 128."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T16:23:28", "task": "M5-T04 full-game bot soak + engine fixes", "status": "ok", "note": "Milestone 5d - new game-core/src/ai/soak.test.ts (3 tests) plays all 8 scenarios x 3 seeds with 4 hard bots and asserts card CONSERVATION (every registered instance in exactly one zone / attached / removed, no id in two zones), sanity (pools >= 0, HP bounded, Outbreak infection 0..3), termination agreement with checkWin, and a natural-end rate floor; plus determinism on the three expansion scenarios and pile/mansion card resolution against the scenario card pool. sim.ts SimConfig gained scenario/cards/piles/mansionCards/outbreakMode/partnerMode so the soak drives the REAL scenario (the old default used the fallback mansion instead of the registry one). The soak found SIX real defects, all fixed: (1) starting-deck instance ids collided across seats (4 seats dealt the same am-001#1..#7, so state.cards could only name one of four physical cards) - ids are now seat-scoped; (2) revive used a plain draw, so a downed character with a short inventory came back with fewer than 5 cards (rulebook: draw 5 with reshuffle) and the redraw destroyed any cards an effect had given the downed player; (3) a card listed by two piles (alliance we-004 in knife-plain + melee-combat) registered the SAME instances twice, putting one card in two piles - setup now mints pile-scoped ids and the redundant data pile was removed; (4) prompts built from an empty zone had ZERO options, which gates every action behind resolve-pending-prompt and deadlocks the seat (bots threw, a human UI would render an empty dialog) - new engine/prompts.ts dropEmptyPrompts choke point in applyAction + startTurn, plus guards on the Leon builders; (5) Outbreak reanimation shuffled hand+discard+inventory but DROPPED the Play Area, destroying every card played that turn - now included; (6) the greedy bot skipped every turn forever on PR-002 Jill (skip ships the hand to discard, revaluing cards from held 0.5x to owned 1x, and the sim kept the turn pools) - policy now clamps the discard for every non-buy simulation and treats the skip option as turn-ending, so seeds 1-8 all end naturally (rate 0.264 vs 0.271 baseline). New engine/m5-regressions.test.ts (4 tests) pins the mechanisms. cardsForScenario/isExpansionScenario added to game-core and consumed by server host.ts + client hotseat.ts (was a duplicated inline mapping). Gates: typecheck exit 0, game-core 533, server 96, client 128."}
